com/users/yangqunfeng/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2024-12-29T08:55:11Z", "updated_at": "2024-12-29T08:55:11Z", "body": "**Ardupilot** is using Copter-4.5.6, and below are the specific parameters of the flight controller.\r\n[6011.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18268933/6011.zip)\r\n\r\n**MAVSDK** is currently using versions 2.12.3 and 2.13.0.\r\nThe **hardware** is CUAV X7+, with a custom expansion board.\r\nThe logic of my code is as follows:\r\nFirst, I use the **subscribe_on_new_system** function, which is used to callback when the flight controller connects and disconnects. Then, I create a telemetry service, but also connect to the drone through passthrough, and I set the message intervals for the following messages using MAV_CMD_SET_MESSAGE_INTERVAL. The key is the message ID, and the value is the message interval.\r\n`const std::vector<std::pair<uint32_t, float>> message_intervals = {\r\n        {MAVLINK_MSG_ID_GPS_RAW_INT, 500000.0f},\r\n        {MAVLINK_MSG_ID_GLOBAL_POSITION_INT, 500000.0f},\r\n        {MAVLINK_MSG_ID_ATTITUDE, 500000.0f},\r\n        {MAVLINK_MSG_ID_MISSION_CURRENT, 1000000.0f},\r\n        {MAVLINK_MSG_ID_BATTERY_STATUS, 1000000.0f},\r\n        {MAVLINK_MSG_ID_STATUSTEXT, 1000000.0f},\r\n        {MAVLINK_MSG_ID_POWER_STATUS, 1000000.0f},\r\n};\r\n`\r\nI have created the corresponding callback functions to receive messages such as **Global Position** and **Raw Position**, and I check whether the position information is being returned at the specified frequency. By the way (a side note), when I previously used MAVSDK version 2.0.1, when I detected that the drone hadn't sent the subscribed messages for a while, I would again use MAV_CMD_SET_MESSAGE_INTERVAL to resubscribe to the messages. Although the drone would occasionally disconnect, it didn't happen as frequently as it does now.\r\nI am sure the issue might be with my program, mainly because the QGC (Ground Control Station) doesn't show the drone disconnecting, but my program does.\r\nI also want to ask if the message intervals I\u2019ve set are feasible, particularly {MAVLINK_MSG_ID_GPS_RAW_INT, 500000.0f} and {MAVLINK_MSG_ID_GLOBAL_POSITION_INT, 500000.0f}. I previously encountered situations where gps_fix_type was no_gps and global_position_health was false, but it was actually rtk_fix. I improved this issue by increasing the message interval and having MP (Mission Planner) actively send message groups.\r\nThank you for your response as the main maintainer of the MAVSDK project. This is very important to me. I appreciate your patient explanation.", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/2564657284/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null, "event": "commented", "actor": {"login": "yangqunfeng", "id": 20263333, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjYzMzMz", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20263333?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng", "html_url": "https://github.com/yangqunfeng", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/2565258092", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2486#issuecomment-2565258092", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2486", "id": 2565258092, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBabE0s6Y5rts", "user": {"login": "yangqunfeng", "id": 20263333, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjIwMjYzMzMz", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20263333?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng", "html_url": "https://github.com/yangqunfeng", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangqunfeng/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2024-12-30T09:53:05Z", "updated_at": "2024-12-30T09:53:05Z", "body": "Today, I discovered again that the serial port automatically reconnects after about 10 minutes, with the following prompt:\r\nDiscovered 1 